# date:      2026-09-19T07:24:40Z
# machine:   4 vCPU, Intel(R) Xeon(R) Processor @ 2.10GHz
# commit:    d7c5a04
# R13:       this machine's Rust crossing is 2.1 ns (fwd+reverse) to 2.8 ns
#            (forward), against 1.8 ns on the Rust slice's container.
#            See 00-r13-rust-crossing.log. Quote every absolute below
#            against it as well as in nanoseconds.

# Absolutes across these blocks are NOT comparable to each other in the way
# a within-process ratio is: they are four processes. What they establish is
# whether the SHAPE of the answer (which mechanism wins, by how much) holds
# across 3.10 to 3.13, which is what README open question 4 needs.

